WEBVTT

00:06:58.156 --> 00:07:00.236
So you've got to cut,
become more efficient,

00:07:00.236 --> 00:07:03.436
and then Lindsay, then people
can rely on carbon removal.

00:07:03.436 --> 00:07:07.556
But when you look at all the models
from IPCC or even our rough modeling,

00:07:07.596 --> 00:07:09.956
you're still going to have
10 gigatons left over.

00:07:09.956 --> 00:07:12.756
And so we've got to invest
in carbon-removal technologies

00:07:12.796 --> 00:07:15.596
that are both nature-based
as well as engineered,

00:07:15.596 --> 00:07:17.716
because we're going to
need it in the future.

00:07:17.756 --> 00:07:18.956
LL: Climate justice.

00:07:18.956 --> 00:07:20.556
Let's talk about climate justice.

00:07:20.556 --> 00:07:21.996
It's a big theme in the book.

00:07:21.996 --> 00:07:25.516
John, you are an affluent white American,

00:07:25.516 --> 00:07:27.476
white male American.

00:07:28.276 --> 00:07:30.076
Yay, exactly.